Instead of having an X86DecodeFunc for each opcode map, just use
the map number as the entry point in the generated bytecode, and
let decode_insn() run the program from there.  Remove the #defines that
were used to shorten the declarations for opcode entries.

Signed-off-by: Paolo Bonzini <pbonzini@redhat.com>
