 target/i386/tcg/decode-new.h     |   9 +-
 target/i386/tcg/decode-new.c.inc | 281 +++----------------------------
 2 files changed, 32 insertions(+), 258 deletions(-)

diff --git a/target/i386/tcg/decode-new.h b/target/i386/tcg/decode-new.h
index 3fe7a483301..f7424d4d33e 100644
--- a/target/i386/tcg/decode-new.h
+++ b/target/i386/tcg/decode-new.h
@@ -300,10 +300,11 @@ struct DisasContext;
  * Decoding the opcode runs a small program that starts after the legacy,
  * REX, REX2, VEX and EVEX prefixes have been consumed, and that walks a
  * trie whose leaves are rows of a table of X86OpEntry structs.  There is
- * one entry point for each opcode map: 0 for the one-byte opcodes, 1 for
- * 0F, 2 for 0F38, 3 for 0F3A and 4-7 for the EVEX maps.  The bytecode
- * interpreter is invoked from X86DecodeFuncs, for example decode_0F()
- * can invoke decode_run() for any of maps 1..3.
+ * one entry point for each opcode map, at steps 0-7 of the program: 0 for
+ * the one-byte opcodes, 1 for 0F, 2 for 0F38, 3 for 0F3A and 4-7 for the
+ * EVEX maps.  disas_insn() reads the 0F/0F38/0F3A escapes as part of,
+ * prefix handling, fetching everything up to the first opcode byte before
+ * running the program.
  *
  * The program can look at:
  * - b, the last opcode byte that was fetched
